    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1938644635905303020",
      "url": "https://x.com/songs349/status/1938644635905303020",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/songs349/status/1938644635905303020",
      "text": "The JSDF has revealed details about their participation in Talisman Sabre 2025: https://t.co/fqVFzeXwrJ (translation below).\n\n[Translation]\nParticipation in the U.S.- and Australia-led Multinational Joint Exercise Talisman Sabre 25\n\nThe Japan Self-Defense Forces (JSDF) will participate in the U.S.- and Australia-led multinational joint exercise Talisman Sabre 25 as outlined below. This exercise, co-hosted by the United States and Australia, has been held biennially since 2005 and will mark its 11th iteration. For the JSDF, this will be the sixth participation since its first involvement in 2015. Through this exercise, the JSDF aims to maintain and enhance its joint operational capabilities while strengthening cooperation with participating nations to contribute to the creation of a desirable security environment for Japan.\n\nDetails\n\nObjective:\nTo participate in the U.S.- and Australia-led multinational joint exercise Talisman Sabre 25, enhance and maintain the JSDF’s joint operational capabilities, strengthen cooperation and trust with the armed forces of the U.S., Australia, and other Indo-Pacific countries, and contribute to regional peace and stability.\n\nPeriod (planned):\nFrom Sunday, July 13 to Monday, August 4, 2025\nLocationAustralia (Queensland and New South Wales) and surrounding maritime and airspace areas\nParticipating countries (excluding Japan)United States, Australia, Canada, Fiji, France, Germany, India, Indonesia, Netherlands, New Zealand, Norway, Papua New Guinea, the Philippines, Singapore, South Korea, Thailand, Tonga, and the United Kingdom\n\nParticipating JSDF units:\nApproximately 1,500 personnel from \n- the Joint Staff Office; \n- Joint Operations Command; \n- Ground Staff Office;\n- Ground Component Command;\n- JGSDF Eastern Army;\n- JGSDF Central Army; \n- JGSDF Western Army\n- JGSDF Fuji School;\n- JGSDF Air Defense Artillery School;\n- Maritime Staff Office;\n- JMSDF Fleet Escort Force;\n-  Air Staff Office;\n- JASDF Air Defense Command;\n- JASDF Space Operations Group;\n- Iruma JSDF Hospital;\n- JASDF Logistics Headquarters; \n- Izumo-class destroyer JS Ise;\n- JS Suzunami;\n- Tank landing ship JS Ōsumi\n\nExercise components:\n(1) Maritime operations training\n(2) Amphibious operations training\n(3) Land combat training\n(4) Live-fire training\n(5) Space operations training\n(6) Joint medical support training",
